WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.080
iron rusts from disuse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:11.360
water loses its purity from stagnation even&nbsp;
so does an action sap the vigor of the mind

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.640
time stays long enough for anyone who will use it

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.920
poor is the pupil who does not surpass his master

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.880
there are three classes of people those who see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.240
those who see when they are&nbsp;
shown those who do not see

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.640
i am not poor poor are&nbsp;
those who desire many things

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.280
our life is made by the death of others

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.240
wisdom is the daughter of experience

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:11.840
reprove your friend in secret&nbsp;
and praise him in public

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.320
god sells us all things at the price of labor

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:26.400
as a well-spent day brings happy sleep&nbsp;
so a life well spent brings happy death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:39.840
patience serves as a protection against&nbsp;
wrongs as clothes do against cold

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.120
learning never exhausts the mind

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:57.360
tears come from the heart and not from the brain&nbsp;
while i thought that i was learning how to live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.800
i have been learning how to die

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.440
the greatest deception men&nbsp;
suffer is from their own opinions

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.760
he who walks straight rarely falls

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.360
just as food eaten without&nbsp;
appetite is a tedious nourishment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:31.200
so does study without zeal damage the&nbsp;
memory by not assimilating what it absorbs

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:41.040
marriage is like putting your hand into a bag&nbsp;
of snakes in the hope of pulling out an eel

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:55.360
he who can copy can do he who wishes to&nbsp;
be rich in a day will be hanged in a year

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.840
just as courage imperils life fear protects it

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.800
he who thinks little airs much

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:17.840
all knowledge which ends in words&nbsp;
will die as quickly as it came to life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:24.080
with the exception of the written&nbsp;
word which is its mechanical part

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.840
he who does not punish evil commands it to be done

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:45.840
it is an acknowledged fact that we perceive errors&nbsp;
in the work of others more readily than in our own

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:53.040
no counsel is more trustworthy than that&nbsp;
which is given upon ships that are in peril

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.840
he who does not value life does not deserve it

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.920
beauty perishes in life but is immortal in art

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.840
he who possesses most must be most afraid of loss

